{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Setting up evo.videostroll",
  "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8099/quickstart.html",
  "goal": "Someone who has never seen the project can install it, register it with their agent, and record their first walkthrough.",
  "audience": "A developer who has just cloned the repository and wants it working.",
  "viewport": {
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080
  },
  "voice": {
    "provider": "edge",
    "name": "en-US-JennyNeural"
  },
  "captions": "both",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "what",
      "chapter": "What it is",
      "narration": "This is evo dot videostroll. An agent records a narrated walkthrough of a website, and this page is how you set it up.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "move",
          "target": {
            "selector": "h1"
          }
        }
      ],
      "minDurationMs": 4500
    },
    {
      "id": "prereqs",
      "chapter": "What you need",
      "narration": "You need Node twenty or newer, and nothing else. The video encoder ships inside the package, so there is no separate install.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#prereqs"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "move",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#prereqs h2"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "install",
      "chapter": "Install",
      "narration": "Clone the repository and install from inside the server folder. The browser download is a one off.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#install"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#install pre:first-of-type"
          },
          "holdMs": 1800
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test",
      "narration": "Run the tests before wiring anything up. All one hundred and five of them run offline.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "move",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#install pre:last-of-type"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#install pre:last-of-type"
          },
          "holdMs": 1500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "register",
      "chapter": "Register it",
      "narration": "One command registers the server for every project on the machine. Check it took, and look for the word Connected.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#register"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#register pre:first-of-type"
          },
          "holdMs": 2000
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "skill",
      "chapter": "The skill",
      "narration": "The server records. The skill is what makes the recording worth watching, so copy it into your skills folder.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#skill"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#skill pre"
          },
          "holdMs": 1800
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "current",
      "chapter": "Keeping it current",
      "narration": "Later, one command keeps this machine current. A pull alone is not enough, because the built server and the copied skill both live outside git.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#current"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#current pre"
          },
          "holdMs": 2200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "use",
      "chapter": "Ask for one",
      "narration": "That is the whole setup. Start a session and ask for a walkthrough in plain words.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#use"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#use pre"
          },
          "holdMs": 2200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "login",
      "chapter": "Behind a login",
      "narration": "For a site behind a sign in, you sign in yourself once and it keeps the session. This is the one step that needs a full browser, and it tells you if it cannot find one.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#login"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#login pre:first-of-type"
          },
          "holdMs": 2000
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "batch",
      "chapter": "Re-cut, do not redo",
      "narration": "Every recording also writes the storyboard that produced it. When the site changes, edit the steps that changed and render again.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#batch"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#batch pre"
          },
          "holdMs": 1800
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "output",
      "chapter": "What comes out",
      "narration": "Out comes the video, captions aligned to the spoken words, a manifest of every step, and a still for each one.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#output"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "move",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#output .grid"
          },
          "durationMs": 1200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "voices",
      "chapter": "Voices",
      "narration": "Three providers, and three hundred voices to choose from. List them by locale and gender, and let a single step speak in its own.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "scroll",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#voices"
          },
          "durationMs": 900
        },
        {
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": {
            "selector": "#voices pre"
          },
          "holdMs": 2000
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
